how do you figure out your passion in  life so I got a great question for my  YouTube viewers who love you guys Rob  who wrote in to say hi Evan how do you  figure out what your passion is are in  life this is a great question I want to  get asked a lot and as a result I  created an entire zuga guy to help walk  you through how to find your passion and  turn it into a business but to quickly  summarize if you have no idea what your  passion is if you feel like you want to  do something different with your life  you don't like your job you don't like  working wherever you're working and you  feel like you know I want to do  something meaningful but I have no idea  what it is that I love then you need to  explore you need to take time to explore  because often the ideas that come up  through exploration are not the ones are  gonna make the most sense the most  logical sense so let me give you an  example right now I'm an investor and  owner of a salsa dancing company here in  Toronto we teach five six thousand  people a year how to dance salsa and I  became an instructor and a DJ and owner  in the business when I first got into  salsa it was just out of exploration  right I loved ballroom dancing when I  was in university I went with my  girlfriend at the time and she didn't  like it so we stopped and then when we  broke up like hey this is my chance to  go dancing again and I went to go salsa  if I went and looked at that as a  business opportunity right from the  start I would say this is a stupid idea  right like Evan you know nothing about  salsa zero you didn't learn the dance  growing up so you're way behind right  like people have done this almost from  birth like they're learning the music  they're learning the steps and Here I am  you know my 20s starting from scratch I  didn't speak Spanish I didn't know the  music I was too tall right I take big  steps all these thing is going against  me and if I went into that thinking this  is asking  business opportunity I'm rushing the  finite passion turn into a company by  winning with that attitude it wouldn't  have worked I would have done one class  say this isn't a business it won't work  for me and I would have gotten on  something else but because I approached  it just from an opportunity to explore  and see what I enjoy doing I had a lot  of fun I sucked at it I sucked so bad at  at the start but I loved it I love the  people of the community I love the music  I just fell in love with it and it  became a business opportunity for me so  if you have no idea  don't rush into something don't struggle  and stress yourself out to find  something right now because you're  probably gonna make the wrong decision  and I don't want that for you but I want  you to make the wrong decision and put  your money time effort into something  that's not gonna work out because you  rushed into it too quickly so take your  time to explore try different things you  know I tried snowboarding and I loved it  and then I just started to fall a little  bit but I still enjoyed going  I tried rock climbing and I hated it I  went once that was it I haven't gone  back since but I tried it so won't try  something you're interested buy  something try it out get some experience  see if you fall in love with it and if  you do then look for business  opportunity around it that's my advice  believe for those you're watching let me  know how you found your passion let me  know what you're up to leave a comment  underneath because your experiences and  stories can help inspire other  entrepreneurs as well you like this  video thumbs up below click on my face  subscribe to the channel thank you so  much I'll see you soon  you
 

